            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Nefertiti's Early Life</strong><br>\nNefertiti, whose name means \"the beautiful one has come,\" was born around 1370 BCE. Little is known about her early years before she became queen. Historians believe she may have been of noble birth but not royal, possibly the daughter of a high official named Ay. She married Amenhotep IV, who later changed his name to Akhenaten, and together they started a religious revolution in Egypt.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Nefertiti's Role as Queen</strong><br>\nAs queen, Nefertiti played a significant role in Egypt's cultural and religious life. She was often depicted in temple carvings, showing her importance in religious practices. Under her husband's reign, they established the worship of the sun disk Aten as the primary deity, diminishing the role of the traditional Egyptian pantheon.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Religious Changes in Egypt</strong><br>\nThe reign of Nefertiti and Akhenaten was marked by a drastic shift in Egyptian religion. They introduced the worship of one god, Aten, and closed temples dedicated to other gods. This monotheistic approach was radical for the time and changed Egyptian society, which had traditionally worshiped many gods.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
